    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d471">

                <pb facs="0437" n="[363]" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg363"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Clay to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 63.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">St. Petersburg, Russia,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-11-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 22, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch No. 683 (circular) is
                    received, for which I thank you. I have this morning telegraphic news of the
                    re-election of A. Lincoln as President. I feel that our country is now secure of
                    the future; that slavery will be abolished, the Union restored, and that we will
                    henceforth take our true position in the world as the leaders in all liberalism
                    in fact, as we have heretofore been in theory. * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. M. CLAY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon, <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
